; Common-prime removal for arbitrary positive power exponents.
; The actual prime divides the third coordinate; all quotient equations
; are retained. Nonzero power cancellation preserves the equation, all
; reduced coordinates are nonzero, and the third is strictly smaller.
; Native adaptation of S_FreyPackage_of_counterexample.lean:17-29,
; using positive-Nat prime descent instead of the generic integer gcd API.
